{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781149562,"nonce":"WlarsjtdIVHooZL3UUzYtauvZ6g=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFGOC_g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/252","origin":"github"},"title":"bizzyboat: add _nadir TF frame for garmin_sidescan nadir-depth Range (+X down)","message":"## Add a `_nadir` TF frame for the Garmin sidescan nadir-depth `Range`\n\nThe `garmin_sidescan` driver now decodes the GCV chartplotter's nadir bottom\ndepth from the `:50050` status broadcast and publishes it on `~/nadir_depth` as\n**`sensor_msgs/Range`** (rolker/marine_tools#16, validated against the M3 on the\n2026-06-10 deployment, rolker/unh_echoboats_project11#250).\n\n`sensor_msgs/Range` measures its range **along the frame's +X axis**. But our\nsidescan beam frames use **+Z** as the range axis — `sidescan.xacro` sets\n`bizzy/garmin_sidescan_down` to **+Z down** (the marine convention the\n`RawSonarImage` channels and M3/DeltaT use). So the depth `Range` **cannot reuse\n`_down`** — it needs its own frame whose **+X points down**.\n\nThe driver derives the frame name as `\u003cframe_id\u003e_nadir`, i.e.\n**`bizzy/garmin_sidescan_nadir`** (driver `frame_id` is `bizzy/garmin_sidescan`,\nset in `bizzyboat_project11/launch/sidescan_launch.py`). That frame does not\nexist yet, so the published `Range` currently has no transform.\n\n### Task\n\nIn `bizzyboat_project11/urdf/sensors/sidescan.xacro`, add a `_nadir` link + fixed\njoint to the `garmin_sidescan` macro, co-located with the other beams (same\n`xyz` origin as `_down`) but rotated so **+X points down**:\n\n```xml\n\u003c!-- Nadir depth (sensor_msgs/Range): +X down (Range's range axis is +X,\n     unlike the +Z-down _down beam frame). --\u003e\n\u003clink name=\"bizzy/${name}_nadir\"/\u003e\n\u003cjoint name=\"${name}_to_${name}_nadir\" type=\"fixed\"\u003e\n  \u003cparent link=\"bizzy/${name}\"/\u003e\n  \u003cchild link=\"bizzy/${name}_nadir\"/\u003e\n  \u003corigin xyz=\"0 0 0\" rpy=\"0 ${pi/2} 0\"/\u003e\n\u003c/joint\u003e\n```\n\n`rpy=\"0 ${pi/2} 0\"` pitches the mount frame (X fwd, Y port, Z up) so its **+X**\npoints down — verify in rviz that the `Range` cone points at the bottom.\n\n### Notes / optional\n\n- No driver launch change is required — the driver auto-derives\n  `bizzy/garmin_sidescan_nadir` (its `nadir_frame_id` param defaults to empty →\n  `\u003cframe_id\u003e_nadir`). Set `nadir_frame_id` explicitly only to override.\n- Optionally set the driver's `nadir_beam_width_rad` (→ `Range.field_of_view`)\n  to the GCV down-look beam width once known, so rviz draws a correct cone.\n- Follow-up to the sidescan-frame work in #238.\n\n### Acceptance\n\n- `bizzy/garmin_sidescan_nadir` exists in the TF tree with +X down.\n- `~/nadir_depth` `Range` transforms cleanly and the cone points at the bottom\n  in rviz on real water.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}